{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","hash":"d9c3ac52b59ebba7728b2dcf43f7b1017df5047a18043228c60af19d59a7c53d","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0155pAZuySzasffgXrt8uE9x","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan shown (4 steps)."}]},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EjX6ZEgFtyyEE7ah72ZR7u","type":"tool_result","content":"From github.com:TheSpaghettiDetective/JusPrin\n * branch                  jusprin-newui-integration -> FETCH_HEAD\n6f459dc81efaf1868b9faeffc7c5f75ebec634df\n2ce50f4df630541695123ab58c5537492f7f441c\n2ce50f4df630541695123ab58c5537492f7f441c\n?? .playwright-mcp/\n2ce50f4df6 Welcome clip: put back the caption labels, as Kenneth decided\nd22abdd883 First launch and File › Import: no Retry on the import result, and plain captions in the welcome clip\ne6ef45798a Keep OrcaSlicer's cloud login in its encrypted file, not the macOS keychain\n6f459dc81e First launch: match the first-run boards (canvas v134) for the sign-up card, the own-account card, the skip note and the import result\nFirst launch and File › Import: no Retry on the import result, and plain captions in the welcome clip\n\nThe OrcaSlicer import result no longer has a \"Retry failed items\" button,\non the first launch or in File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer…. The two\nfailures that can go another way next time now say how to try again on\ntheir own line:\n- a file JusPrin couldn't read: \"JusPrin couldn't read this file. To try\n  again, choose File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer…\"\n- a preset JusPrin couldn't load: \"JusPrin couldn't load this preset. To\n  try again, choose File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer…\"\nA new import from that menu lists the failed printers and presets again,\nbecause JusPrin doesn't have them. The other failures already say what to\ndo or fail the same way every time.\n\nRemoved with the button: the page action onboarding_import_retry (also\nfrom resources/jusprin/home/protocol.json), the File › Import window's\n\"retry\" action, HomeBackend::retry_orca_import, OrcaImporter::retry,\norca_import_retryable, and the \"retryable\" field on each result line.\n\nWelcome clip (resources/jusprin/welcome/welcome-clip.mp4): each beat's\ncaption is now plain text at the lower left in body bold and the secondary\ntext color, as boards first-run-welcome-01 and -02 draw it, instead of a\ndark label. The animatic's source isn't kept, so the captions were\nrepainted into the clip's own YUV frames: only the caption area changed,\nevery other pixel decodes as before. Same size, frame rate and length\n(1240x776, 12 fps, 12.2 s), 503 KB instead of 480 KB. The README beside it\nsays so.\n\nTested: HomeUI vitest 156, AgentUI vitest 692, both tsc runs clean.\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M6S9TBPR2ZM87689QZZX1N5K","is_error":false}]}}
