{"parentUuid":"d8faeb33-a9cb-466b-aa98-c9623d4c2dd7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnRJKmefrKaad18pcr6Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I pushed jusprin-newui-integration: GitHub moved from 6f459dc81e to cf2fae27f8 as a plain fast-forward, and jusprin-newui wasn't touched. Two commits went up:\n\n- **e6ef45798a** keeps the OrcaSlicer cloud login in OrcaSlicer's encrypted file instead of the macOS keychain.\n- **cf2fae27f8** removes the Retry button from the import result, on first launch and in File › Import. A file JusPrin couldn't read, or a preset it couldn't load, now says on its own line to try again from File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer….\n\nBefore pushing, I combined the Retry removal with the commit that put the clip back into one commit. Its files are identical to the old local tip, and it doesn't touch the welcome clip, so the clip keeps the dark \"Show it what happened.\" label you chose. The repainted clip never reached GitHub. The hashes d22abdd883 and 2ce50f4df6 I gave earlier no longer exist; I told the design session the new hash.\n\nA few things are still open:\n- The welcome-clip screenshots 12 and 13 in the shared notes folder show plain captions. They no longer match the app.\n- Until the next cmake build, my local build's Home bundle still holds the plain-caption clip. The committed file is correct.\n- The design for the File › Import result also has the line \"OrcaSlicer's own files were not changed.\" The app doesn't show it yet. It wasn't part of this task."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":245,"cache_read_input_tokens":110712,"output_tokens":562,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":66},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":245,"ephemeral_5m_input